### **Day 31-40: Introduction to NoSQL with MongoDB**  

**Topic:**  
Introduction to NoSQL databases, focusing on MongoDB as a document-based database system.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand the differences between SQL and NoSQL databases.  
• Learn MongoDB document structure and CRUD operations.  
• Explore indexing, aggregation, and replication in MongoDB.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Install MongoDB and connect using MongoDB Shell (mongosh).  
• Perform CRUD operations on sample collections.  
• Create an aggregation pipeline for data analysis.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• Document-oriented storage (JSON/BSON).  
• Horizontal scaling (sharding).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `db.collection.insertOne()` – Insert a document.  
• `db.collection.find()` – Query documents.  
• `db.collection.createIndex()` – Optimize queries.  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Storing user-generated content (e.g., social media posts).  
• Handling large-scale IoT sensor data.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• MongoDB Atlas (Cloud Database).  
• MongoDB Compass (GUI).  

**Summary:**  
Learned MongoDB basics, including document structure, queries, and optimization techniques for scalable NoSQL applications.  

