### **Day 41-50: Server-side with Python Flask & REST APIs**  

**Topic:**  
Building RESTful APIs with Python Flask for database interactions.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Design RESTful endpoints for database operations.  
• Integrate Flask with MongoDB using PyMongo.  
• Implement authentication and error handling.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Develop a Flask API with CRUD functionalities.  
• Secure API endpoints using JWT tokens.  
• Test API endpoints with Postman.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• REST principles (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE).  
• ORM vs. ODM (Object Data Modeling).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• N/A (Using PyMongo: `db.collection.insert_one()`, `db.collection.find()`).  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Backend for mobile/web apps.  
• Microservices architecture.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• Flask (Python Framework).  
• Postman (API Testing).  
• PyMongo (MongoDB Driver).  

**Summary:**  
Built a Flask API to interact with MongoDB, applying REST principles for scalable backend development.  

